Code review of every fix since the last code review. Scope: `git diff c27afaf..72a1066 -- game tools tests` (skip docs/reviews). That is round 1's four fixer branches (launch-from-hold, flash-and-looks, hold-view, ko-respawn-bars), round 2's five (r2-finisher-flash, r2-launch-into-walls, r2-vfx-first-use, r2-player-ko-view, r2-dummy-comeback) and the lead's gap-09 and test change. The code lens last reviewed f43ab9a..c27afaf; nobody has reviewed these diffs, which were built on separate branches and merged into hub files (combat_actor.gd, player.gd, humanoid_rig.gd, ragdoll.gd, training_dummy.gd, enemy_health_bars.gd, tuning.gd, tuning_data.gd, first_person_camera.gd, vfx_director.gd, comic_sprite.gd, damage_look.gd). Use `git log --first-parent c27afaf..72a1066` and each fixer's fix-*.json to see which branch wrote what.
Check, with file:line evidence:
1. Layer rules. Simulation never reads a camera; presentation (cameras, HUD, VFX, audio) only subscribes to CombatEvents and reads state, never writes it (TimeController excepted). In particular: the KO view reads the player's state and never writes it (no writes to the player, its rig's game state or the simulation); the VFX warm-up emits no CombatEvents and touches no game state; the wall take-over is detected in the simulation, not from the ragdoll or a camera; the comeback's 'in the player's view' uses the player's facing, not a camera; CombatActor.impact_frame_ticks() copies VfxDirector's impact-frame rule instead of sharing it (can they drift?).
2. No feel numbers in scripts. Grep the diff for numeric literals in game/. The fixers left some on purpose (_HELD_BLEND_S, _GRAB_EASE_S, the stagger's 0.04 s blend in _apply_reaction()); list every remaining feel number. Each new tunable is an @export_range in the right group and subgroup, is in tuning/default.json, has a ## doc, and is read live: a value cached at _ready or in a const must re-read on Tuning.changed, or be read at use.
3. Static types everywhere, tabs, ## doc comments on new public API, comment density like the surrounding code; stale comments the fixes left (headers and ARCHITECTURE bullets that name 'the one place' something happens, ragdoll.gd's header, humanoid_rig.gd's flash_at doc).
4. Interactions between fixes merged from separate branches. Trace each path in the code and probe it headless where cheap (a scratch GUT test or script under your captures folder; don't edit tracked files):
   - the launch out of a hold (at_once full ragdoll) against grab-02's release into a stagger, and against the new wall take-over (a point-blank throw into a wall must read as it did before round 2);
   - the push's part-body search reading a stale drawn-pose cache (Ragdoll._queue_impulse() before gap-07's seed): what it picks on a dummy's first ragdoll, after set_post() moved it, and after a respawn; whether the approved contact push now depends on an accident;
   - the delayed finisher flash (hit-04) against _vanish and the blink-off (a KO'd body vanishing with a flash pending), against the warm-up, and against the always-on detail layer (perf-02) and set_flash()'s emission;
   - _turn_solid() and the ghost blink-in against the respawn queries, the new ring clearance, the 'wait, don't walk in' rule (return_home's stuck detection) and gap-07's seeded first-tick pose read by _has_room();
   - the KO view against the hold view (KO'd while holding), the get-up's ease back in, F2's camera cycle, the free-fly and side-view debug cameras, a KO in side view, and VIS_FP_HIDDEN restored exactly; its wall and fighter clearance ray;
   - the VFX warm-up with impact_frame_enabled off (no ink frame ever, not even the warm-up pixel), headless (skipped), and pooled sprites returned to the pool;
   - the new reaction-blend tunables against hitstop and slow-mo (the snap must still show through a finisher's hitstop in open space).
5. Tests. Each new test exercises its fix (say where it plainly would pass without it). Judge the lead's 0.8 -> 0.85 change in test_ragdoll.gd's hook arm-trail check: is the sag a real defect of the re-posed arm, or the threshold? Run the full suite (tools/run_tests.sh) and read the whole output for SCRIPT ERROR and ERROR.
6. Docs (findings only, lower priority): docs/ARCHITECTURE.md's VFX, Audio, Ragdoll, Hit flash, hold-view and KO-view sections against the code. List each mismatch with the exact sentence and the code that contradicts it (leg 3 updates the docs).
